This week I made us some French toast, and we ate it with Honeybutter =E3=
=81=8B=E3=82=89 I
titled my email after it! (English-Japanese Grammar Fusion =F0=9F=98=8E=F0=
=9F=92=A3)

August 4th partly cloudy =E2=9B=85=EF=B8=8F

Today was a pretty fun Pday! Here's a little rundown of what we did. As
soon as I woke up in the morning, I took a quick shower and called up my
family earlier than usual from our apartment, so that I could play Magic
the Gathering over video call with Dobberfuhl=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81. It was sup=
er fun to talk
with my family (as always =F0=9F=98=9A) and it was really fun getting to pl=
ay some
Magic too. Elder Dobberfuhl beat me the first game, but I managed to win
the second time. It was great! After that, Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and I=
 headed to Cafe
Gusto for a lunch of pizza and Ice cream (for Me) lol. We also stopped by
the toy store as usual, and I got a pretty cool new Magic card for my deck!
We also got to chat with the lady working at the front desk for a while,
she=E2=80=99s really nice! Doesn't seem like she has much interest, but may=
be we
just need to keep talking with her and praying that she'll feel prompted to
meet with us! Next we stopped by a home improvement store for supplies To
upgrade Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=E2=80=99s nunchucks. Now they are attach=
ed with a real chain
rather than just a faux leather cord. Lastly we got some groceries, (mostly
to make food for our family home evening activity that night) and while we
were at the store I tried out a fun little gumball machine where you
control a platform and guide a gumball up a ramp: if you make it to the top
the machine gives you two or 3 pieces of gum instead of just the one! I did
poorly, and Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 gave it a whirl. He got the gumball =
to the top! His
gumball went into a special hole, and out popped- 1 piece of gum =F0=9F=98=
=82=F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 All
of his meticulous control of the machine and it didn't give him more than
he would've gotten if his gumball fell off the platform immediately lol. I
thought it was hilarious. After that we headed over to the church to wind
down and get some food ready for the family home evening activity. We were
in over our heads. Koumoto=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F doesn't know when to stop talk=
ing =F0=9F=98=82. It was a
great lesson With Him and Nishioka san, but it ended up going until like
10:00 PM =F0=9F=98=A2 We need to try and politely address him about how we =
can try
and do things more efficiently next time =F0=9F=98=85 All in all, a pretty =
good Pday.

August 5th rainy afternoon =F0=9F=8C=A7

Today was awesome! I feel like today we made a big step as far as finding
time (and protecting finding time) goes. We started off the day with DCM,
and I gave a training about how it's important as missionaries to teach for
understanding. I shared about my experiences teaching Nao and Mai with
Sonomura=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81, and how it's important we break things down int=
o manageable
chunks depending on the friends level of comprehension. I also expressed
the importance of our friends=E2=80=99 agency, and how even if we teach per=
fectly,
it's still up for them to let our message into their hearts, and work in
them. It was pretty nice. Afterwards we headed out to do some housing, for
around 2 ish hours. It was pretty dry as far as responses go, but it felt
great to be out doing the work! We were able to get out a lot of flyers and
cards, so it was a success even if we couldn't see it in the moment. Later
we had studies, Media Dendou, and lastly Eikaiwa! It was a really fun
Eikaiwa tonight, and Katayama san, Matsuoka San and I even played some
Boggle together! I really love those two. Afterwards Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=
=80=81 shared a
spiritual Message about the importance of prayer (It's super important!!!
Every day!!!) And we talked and enjoyed some snacks all together. I told
everyone about how I love looking for CDs and got a few tips as to where I
might look. All in all, super great day =F0=9F=98=8A

August 6th Mostly Cloudy =E2=98=81=EF=B8=8F=F0=9F=8C=A5

Dream: Tonight I had some crazy dreams that mostly took place in some Kind
of store. In the front area of the store there was a huge squid that was
kind of encased in the wall and was the power source for something, it was
a squid engine. Another interesting thing was that there was a game
console, and my mom somehow destroyed it, and like threw it into the ocean
as well lol. She was showing me some tiny game consoles that she found, and
a tiny one that fit in a small backpack that Elder Dobberfuhl made. There
was also in the back of the store some construction that went on, and
looking at some past surveillance footage, the workers had to spend hours
and hours stacking up purple hangers.

Very weird dream lol, there was a bunch of other stuff including caves and
spiders but it's all so disconnected its kind of a mess to write it lol.
Also I feel like everything lately is turning purple =F0=9F=9F=AA =F0=9F=98=
=82

Today was a good day! After leaving the apartment today, we went out and
did a solid hour of housing in the morning. It's refreshing to have a
streak of good finding time each day, I'm hoping we can keep up the
momentum for tomorrow as well! We weren't able to see any huge success with
our housing, but we were out and doing the Lord=E2=80=99s work, which is wh=
at
really counts! In the afternoon (after some stew courtesy of Nakazawa=E9=95=
=B7=E8=80=81) I
was able to call my mom and spend some time chatting with her because it
was her birthday! If you remember, I mentioned in the MTC how it was my
mom's birthday and I completely forgot, well=E2=80=A6 Let's just say that i=
f she
didn't send me a message about how she was enjoying her birthday, I have
realized much too late... =F0=9F=98=B5 I can't believe I didn't learn my le=
sson from
last time =F0=9F=98=A2 later today we headed to the church to help Morimoto=
=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 with
Kodomo Eikaiwa (kids english conversation!) This time there were two new
and naughty boys who joined the crowd. It was good, but exhausting, and I'm
sure Morimoto=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 felt it more than we did =F0=9F=98=85 later=
 we did some Media
finding, and headed to bed. The days really do go by quickly =E2=8F=B3=EF=
=B8=8F=F0=9F=AA=BD

August 7th Rainy Morning =F0=9F=8C=A7

Dreamed that I hid in a bathtub and scared my elementary school friend,
dreamed about being at my great grandparents house, and how I defended my
sister from my grandpa

Today we had a great mix of missionary work, and something actually crazy
happened =F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=98=B1

I started off the day by accidentally bonking my head on an overhang in our
apartment, which was nice =F0=9F=99=83 And after some studies we set out to=
 do some
streeting by a small college. Heres where it begins. We are biking around
the college borders, looking for some people to talk with, and suddenly
Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 realized that right now it's summer vacation, so=
 like nobody
would be here. We Press forward regardless, and a minute Of riding out
bikes later, we stop in front of a bike parking lot abd talk to two girls
that were walking by. [Background: Since the start of this week, we've been
watching bits and pieces of a film by our church called =E2=80=9CMeet the M=
ormons=E2=80=9D
during our companion study. While watching it, I had the idea to try a
streeting approach in which we ask people what they think about Christians,
kind of a short survey style question. Back to the story!!] We asked them
what they thought about Christians, and they said Christmas is the first
thing that comes to mind. It kind of tapered off and felt a bit forced but
as the two left, a curly haired guy pulled up, and dapped me up as I was
wrapping up our conversation with the two girls. By the way, as this is
happening there's another guy staring at us from his car, kind of circling
us a bit and smiling at the curly haired guy. Super weird lol. Anyways, we
talk with Curly and ask what he thinks about Christians. He was super open
with us, and said he wasn't opposed to joining a church, but he didn't
really have any reason to, as he doesn't know much about church in general.
Then the guy who circled us before pulled up and joined in our
conversation. They were both insanely chill, probably partly cause they're
both our age. Anyways, they asked if we're asking a lot of people the
survey, and we said yes. Then=E2=80=A6 they pretty much walked us inside of=
 the
university right into the middle of the main study hall with like 100+
college students all preparing for a test =F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=98=
=B1 They pretty much told us
to go around table to table and ask everyone the questions, they were
insanely supportive and wanted to help us out. Everyone was staring at us
from the second we walked I'm, so it was hard to be calm lol. We talked
with like 30 different people about what they know about Christians, almost
nobody knew much about Christians, and nobody had seen missionaries like us
before. The two that brought us in also took a bunch of our flyers and
cards and passed them out to everyone, get these two missionary nametags
already =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 After some time they kinda esc=
orted us out in a hurry, I
think their test was about to start. After we were outside, we even got to
talk with one of their professors! He was also super nice and talked with
us, it was incredible. In the end we didn't get Either of the Two=E2=80=99s=
 contact
info which SUUUUUCKS but they have our number, and hopefully we can see
them again by streeting near the university again! Now a bunch of young
people know our faces, and everyone we talked to seemed to like us and have
some level of interest in even just talking with us. It was insane. Still
can't get over this. The two guys also took a BeReal with us and a bunch of
photos and videos, I need to meet them again if not just to get the vids
lol =F0=9F=98=82 Later today we got some more flyers printed and passed the=
m out for
around an hour while housing. One thing that stuck out was one nice lady.
We knocked on her door, and as she opened it up, a huge wasp flew inside.
She managed to smack it back outside with her hand, but she was super sweet
and even asked where I'm from. (It's like super rare to have someone ask a
question to us while housing btw) She didn't have any interest in Eikaiwa,
Game Night, Or the Gospel, but she was very sweet. She even popped her head
out the window as we left to inform us that her neighbor wasn't home, so
they wouldn't answer the door. Super sweet! Afterwards we studied the Book
of Mormon at the church a little bit and then headed off to Japanese class
at the community center. Before our meeting started, I talked a lot with
one of the teachers, and taught her some English. I also made a joke Which
cracked her up. (I've been making so many Jokes recently! I'm trying to get
better at it lol) She was really sweet, and it was so fun to talk. She
really reminds me of my mom, which is a big plus =E2=9E=95=EF=B8=8F Class w=
ent well, we
Ended up talking a decent bit about old technology, like floppy Disks (I'm
looking at you Dad!) The Teacher was amazed that I knew about Floppy disks
and 8 track recording stuff, Because nobody else really did haha. I'm
grateful for what my Dad taught me :) Today was a huge miracle ^_^ One neat
thing was that Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 was inspired, and felt like we sh=
ould Go over by
the college for finding, however, if we tried just a normal approach like
usual, we would have never gotten to have that experience meeting so many
college students. It was only because we were both inspired (by God!) and
acted upon it that we were able to see such a huge miracle. I=E2=80=99m so
grateful.

August 8th Rainy Afternoon =F0=9F=8C=A7
Today we had our weekly planning and Game night. For game night Nishioka
San and Matsuoka San both showed up, and Nishioka san brought a bunch of
sweets. Cheesecake, Ice cream, and then a couple packs of yogurt randomly
lol. It was super fun playing Uno, I think we only had like 2 full games
before the spiritual thought, I won both times =F0=9F=98=8A Theres Definite=
ly more to
Uno than just luck, because I think my luck is generally bad so the only
other option is that I'm incredibly talented =F0=9F=98=8A hehe. Anyways, I =
shared a
spiritual message, and I felt the spirit so strongly, especially as I
prayed for the two of our friends at the end. I hope that in this next week
or two we can see more growth with them!

Poetry Ky=C5=ABkei (break)

=E4=BD=90=E7=94=A8=E3=81=B8

=E4=BD=90=E7=94=A8=E3=81=AA=E3=82=89
=E7=A7=81=E3=81=9F=E3=81=A1=E3=81=A8=E3=81=AF
=E3=82=B5=E3=83=A8=E3=83=8A=E3=83=A9=E3=81=A0

Neon Lights in the
Rain dripping down the window
Of my one-way train.

As I stare at my
Reflection, I try to see
Your face. But, I can't.

This next thing isn't poetry, just an interesting thought I had:
I believe that God has given us our lives and trials as a way to learn and
grow and become like him one day, but it made me wonder if God still
learns. Can a supreme being with all the knowledge of the universe possibly
still learn? I think the answer is yes, but I don't have any real way to
know for sure at the moment. Here's an example: If you memorize a book,
then you could probably say you =E2=80=9Cknow=E2=80=9D everything written i=
n the book. But
from the Book, you can still have new ideas, and =E2=80=9Cgrow=E2=80=9D in =
that sense I
think. I bet that our Heavenly Father can see and maybe even learn a bit
from our experiences! It's said that the teacher can even learn from the
student, the parent can learn from the child. We are His children after all=
!

August 9th Suddenly Rainy =F0=9F=95=91=F0=9F=8C=A7=F0=9F=8C=A7

Dream about guitar, headphones, mine craft, neighbors driveway, milk and
cereal, playing sax instrument with strings too, Elder Dobberfuhl got a 100
yen coin out of an arcade machine

Today was pretty odd, but really good. We started out our day by heading
over to the Morimoto=E2=80=99s house to do some more weeding. It was awesom=
e, they
were super grateful. We went inside and had some super tasty Udon with a
bunch of cool flavors and healthy ingredients, and even some ice cream!! It
was awesome. After we ate, we had a short Mogi (roleplay) invitation to
church, and had a prayer together. I love the Morimotos. Morimoto=E5=A7=89=
=E5=A6=B9 also
reminds me of my mom so I feel at home in their home =F0=9F=98=81 Kindness =
and
hospitality speak volumes!
Later today due to the rain we were kinda stuck in the church doing some
Facebook finding, but later that day we were able to go and play Volleyball
with a bunch of young people around our age. They were all so good! I was
very rusty. We got to talk a lot with a guy named Towa and a girl named
Yuzuki. Hopefully we will have good experiences with them in the future!

August 10th Unconditionally Rainy =F0=9F=8C=A7=F0=9F=8C=A7=F0=9F=8C=A7

Dreamed about a huge house with some weird carpet and a huge attic space,
dreamed about waiting in line and spilling my tiny dice all over =F0=9F=98=
=AD=F0=9F=98=82

Today was an awesome Sacrament meeting! The Imai couple visited from
Takahashi, and they shared some amazing testimonies. There was also a
